WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:02.600 --> 00:06.000
National Radio and Television Administration.

3
01:25.000 --> 01:30.000
Welcome to Sister Pang's Bathhouse.

4
01:39.440 --> 01:40.759
Mr. Han, Mrs. Han.

5
01:42.200 --> 01:43.729
I have to be honest with you.

6
01:43.840 --> 01:46.570
This is my first time handling an insurance case.

7
01:47.680 --> 01:49.160
Although it's her first time,

8
01:49.160 --> 01:50.440
with Lawyer Xiao's

9
01:50.440 --> 01:51.520
professional ability,

10
01:51.520 --> 01:53.400
she can handle all types of cases.

11
01:53.800 --> 01:56.520
Mr. Dong said you've handled many big cases.

12
01:56.520 --> 01:57.320
Our case

13
01:57.320 --> 01:59.039
shouldn't be a problem for you.

14
01:59.039 --> 01:59.840
Mr. Dong.

15
02:07.560 --> 02:10.120
The main thing is I have to be responsible for you.

16
02:10.120 --> 02:12.120
Lawyer Xiao, please,

17
02:14.040 --> 02:16.640
try your best to fight for us.

18
02:17.440 --> 02:18.700
I just want this matter

19
02:20.079 --> 02:22.010
to be resolved as soon as possible.

20
02:26.240 --> 02:28.760
Bowen, you've handled insurance cases before, right?

21
02:28.760 --> 02:30.920
Yes, I did a few before joining your team.

22
02:30.920 --> 02:32.800
I represented the insurance companies.

23
02:32.800 --> 02:33.680
Didn't you lose all of them?

24
02:33.680 --> 02:34.480
Shut up.

25
02:35.040 --> 02:36.280
You just have to talk, don't you?

26
02:36.280 --> 02:38.680
Isn't failed experience still experience?

27
02:38.680 --> 02:39.840
That's why I always say,

28
02:39.840 --> 02:42.120
it's hard for insurance companies nowadays.

29
02:42.120 --> 02:43.560
I saw online

30
02:43.640 --> 02:44.920
that because the economy is bad,

31
02:44.920 --> 02:47.480
more and more people are committing insurance fraud.

32
02:47.480 --> 02:50.000
After all, human nature can't stand the test.

33
02:50.000 --> 02:52.480
So now the law on personal accident insurance stipulates

34
02:52.480 --> 02:55.040
that the maximum payout for children under ten is 200,000 yuan.

35
02:55.040 --> 02:55.800
Exactly.

36
02:56.040 --> 02:58.040
Having a child costs tens of thousands now.

37
02:58.040 --> 03:00.480
If the child suddenly dies in an accident,

38
03:00.840 --> 03:03.080
they could get hundreds of thousands or even a million.

39
03:03.080 --> 03:05.880
Many people can't resist that kind of temptation.

40
03:06.240 --> 03:08.040
Have you seen that video online?

41
03:08.080 --> 03:10.080
It's about a couple getting on a ship.

42
03:10.080 --> 03:11.960
They were so loving. They went on a trip,

43
03:11.960 --> 03:13.800
and as soon as they got on the deck, the man

44
03:13.800 --> 03:14.600
pushed the woman off.

45
03:14.600 --> 03:16.880
Lawyer Li, what do you think of this case?

46
03:20.720 --> 03:22.650
We are currently on the defensive.

47
03:23.320 --> 03:25.520
The other side is likely to attack from anywhere.

48
03:25.520 --> 03:26.600
So our team

49
03:27.120 --> 03:29.079
needs to study the insurance contract carefully

50
03:29.079 --> 03:30.840
to see what weak points they might target.

51
03:30.840 --> 03:31.800
Understood, Lawyer Li.

52
03:31.800 --> 03:33.240
I will definitely perform well this time.

53
03:33.240 --> 03:34.370
Meeting adjourned.

54
03:35.600 --> 03:36.720
What were you just saying?

55
03:36.720 --> 03:38.640
You really haven't seen that video?

56
03:38.640 --> 03:40.040
I'll send you that video.

57
03:53.440 --> 03:54.200
What are you doing?

58
03:54.200 --> 03:55.440
Delivering water.

59
03:55.520 --> 03:56.440
So many words.

60
03:56.760 --> 03:57.160
It's fine.

61
03:57.160 --> 03:58.240
This insurance company

62
03:58.240 --> 03:59.000
is the best at making a scene.

63
03:59.000 --> 04:00.680
We'll definitely crush them once we make a move.

64
04:00.680 --> 04:02.320
Stop making a fuss here.

65
04:02.320 --> 04:03.200
It's so annoying.

66
04:03.200 --> 04:04.200
Don't be annoyed.

67
04:04.440 --> 04:06.440
Who asked us to be top players in the legal field?

68
04:06.440 --> 04:08.840
With great power comes great responsibility.

69
04:08.840 --> 04:10.400
Are you trying to flatter me to death?

70
04:10.400 --> 04:11.840
This is all from the bottom of my heart.

71
04:11.840 --> 04:13.320
What do you mean by excessive praise?

72
04:13.320 --> 04:14.000
Give it a rest.

73
04:14.000 --> 04:14.840
If you ask me,

74
04:15.040 --> 04:17.320
if even Sister Long can't win this case,

75
04:17.320 --> 04:18.480
then anyone else would lose too.

76
04:18.480 --> 04:19.440
Have some sunflower seeds.

77
04:19.440 --> 04:21.279
Look at the bad habit you've given him.

78
04:21.279 --> 04:22.480
He just opens his mouth and flatters.

79
04:22.480 --> 04:23.680
Are you sincere?

80
04:23.680 --> 04:25.360
Yes, absolutely sincere.

81
04:25.360 --> 04:27.360
Lawyer Xiao definitely won't lose.

82
04:28.760 --> 04:32.080
Besides, insurance cases favor the policyholder.

83
04:33.720 --> 04:35.520
According to the Insurance Law of the People's Republic of China,

84
04:35.520 --> 04:36.520
Article 30,

85
04:36.640 --> 04:38.520
if standard clauses provided by the insurer are used

86
04:38.520 --> 04:39.840
to conclude an insurance contract,

87
04:39.840 --> 04:41.440
and the insurer and the policyholder,

88
04:41.440 --> 04:43.120
the insured or the beneficiary

89
04:43.120 --> 04:44.640
have a dispute over the contract clauses,

90
04:44.640 --> 04:46.640
they shall be interpreted according to common understanding.

91
04:46.640 --> 04:48.960
If there are two or more interpretations of the contract clauses,

92
04:48.960 --> 04:51.360
the people's court or arbitration institution shall make

93
04:51.360 --> 04:54.890
an interpretation in favor of the insured and the beneficiary.

94
05:03.000 --> 05:05.000
Not bad. You memorized it.

95
05:05.240 --> 05:08.040
Uncle, I can memorize even longer ones.

96
05:08.160 --> 05:09.440
Then do another one.

97
05:09.440 --> 05:12.160
How about Article 600 of the Criminal Law?

98
05:15.280 --> 05:18.440
There are 452 articles in the Criminal Law.

99
05:18.760 --> 05:20.040
You read the Criminal Law every day.

100
05:20.040 --> 05:21.160
Didn't you count how many articles there are?

101
05:21.160 --> 05:22.840
No, I didn't read to the end.

102
05:23.160 --> 05:24.640
I was just bluffing.

103
05:24.640 --> 05:26.320
I wanted to see how well you know it.

104
05:26.320 --> 05:27.440
You're good.

105
05:27.760 --> 05:28.840
Was what he just said correct?

106
05:28.840 --> 05:30.000
Yes, definitely.

107
05:30.000 --> 05:30.480
He memorized it

108
05:30.480 --> 05:31.640
like an AI.

109
05:31.640 --> 05:34.100
But it doesn't completely apply to our case.

110
05:35.320 --> 05:36.880
I'll look into it more.

111
05:36.880 --> 05:39.320
Luo Zhi, you memorized it well.

112
05:39.520 --> 05:40.320
Let's go, sis.

113
05:48.080 --> 05:50.720
Not bad. You don't wear glasses for nothing.

114
05:56.760 --> 05:58.560
You're pretty good.

115
05:59.400 --> 06:01.530
Your movements are a bit exaggerated.

116
06:04.520 --> 06:06.040
Where are you?

117
06:07.200 --> 06:08.600
Sorry, I'm late.

118
06:08.600 --> 06:10.200
Lawyer Xiao.

119
06:10.200 --> 06:11.520
You're late.

120
06:11.520 --> 06:12.200
We were waiting for you. Come, take the seat of honor.

121
06:12.200 --> 06:13.320
Sit down.

122
06:13.640 --> 06:14.640
What do you mean?

123
06:15.040 --> 06:16.370
Are you asking me to pay?

124
06:16.880 --> 06:18.440
You're the star who arrived last.

125
06:18.440 --> 06:20.040
How could I let you pay? I'll pay.

126
06:20.040 --> 06:22.240
Right. You drive a Benz. You should pay.

127
06:23.200 --> 06:24.200
Thanks, Lawyer Li.

128
06:24.200 --> 06:25.660
Here. I didn't add garlic.

129
06:28.200 --> 06:31.520
Since Lawyer Li is paying, I'll order some good wine.

130
06:32.000 --> 06:34.659
Drink less, or you'll have a headache tomorrow.

131
06:34.720 --> 06:35.920
Drink more hot water.

132
06:36.640 --> 06:37.520
You really are...

133
06:37.520 --> 06:39.840
How many years have you two been married?

134
06:39.960 --> 06:42.040
Why are you being so affectionate today?

135
06:42.040 --> 06:42.840
Are you putting on a show for us?

136
06:42.840 --> 06:43.720
Is it any of your business?

137
06:43.720 --> 06:45.440
Are you trying to make us jealous?

138
06:45.440 --> 06:46.400
Let me tell you.

139
06:46.440 --> 06:48.840
This guy had a crush on Zhao Jia in school.

140
06:49.080 --> 06:50.720
But Cheng Fei beat him to it.

141
06:50.720 --> 06:51.360
Lian.

142
06:52.200 --> 06:53.800
You never told me about this.

143
06:53.880 --> 06:54.360
No.

144
06:54.640 --> 06:55.440
Lawyer Li.

145
06:55.440 --> 06:56.840
I'm suing her for defamation.

146
06:56.840 --> 06:57.600
Go ahead.

147
06:57.680 --> 06:58.400
I'm not afraid of you.

148
06:58.400 --> 07:00.200
I have our Lawyer Xiao.

149
07:00.400 --> 07:01.440
Old classmates are the best.

150
07:01.440 --> 07:02.520
Introducing business to me right away.

151
07:02.520 --> 07:03.760
But I charge legal fees.

152
07:03.760 --> 07:04.400
Of course.

153
07:04.400 --> 07:05.930
Just give me a 20% discount.

154
07:06.080 --> 07:07.720
What cases are you two working on lately?

155
07:07.720 --> 07:08.840
An insurance case.

156
07:16.440 --> 07:20.160
Your client wouldn't happen to be Shengkang Insurance, would it?

157
07:21.440 --> 07:23.370
Then your client's surname is Han.

158
07:24.120 --> 07:24.920
Really?

159
07:27.160 --> 07:28.080
How could this...

160
07:28.080 --> 07:30.080
You're debating again, aren't you?

161
07:30.800 --> 07:32.280
What did they argue about when they were in school?

162
07:32.280 --> 07:33.280
Whether that circle was round or not.

163
07:33.280 --> 07:34.480
Anyway, I remember it very clearly.

164
07:34.480 --> 07:37.680
Li Xin said there is no perfect circle in the world.

165
07:38.080 --> 07:41.200
Xiao went to the blackboard and drew a circle by hand.

166
07:41.200 --> 07:43.040
That circle looked like it was drawn with a compass.

167
07:43.040 --> 07:44.840
I wasn't talking about whether it was round or not.

168
07:44.840 --> 07:45.720
What I meant was,

169
07:45.720 --> 07:48.200
there is no absolute fairness and justice in this world,

170
07:48.200 --> 07:49.080
just like there is no

171
07:49.080 --> 07:50.320
perfect circle in this world.

172
07:50.320 --> 07:51.580
Then she just had to...

173
07:51.640 --> 07:54.440
You said that, so what if I draw you another circle?

174
07:54.560 --> 07:55.280
Some things,

175
07:55.280 --> 07:57.200
as long as we pursue them, they exist.

176
07:57.200 --> 07:57.960
Right?

177
07:57.960 --> 07:58.560
Yes.

178
07:58.560 --> 07:59.720
Can you draw it rounder than this pot?

179
07:59.720 --> 08:01.600
Then tell me, is this a perfect circle?

180
08:01.600 --> 08:02.720
I'm talking about objectivity.

181
08:02.720 --> 08:03.400
How is it objective?

182
08:03.400 --> 08:05.080
Is it an objective circle?

183
08:05.080 --> 08:05.840
It's subjective.

184
08:05.840 --> 08:06.800
How is it subjective?

185
08:06.800 --> 08:07.680
It was made.

186
08:07.720 --> 08:08.640
Excuse me.

187
08:09.080 --> 08:10.200
I have a question.

188
08:10.200 --> 08:11.720
It's been bothering me until now.

189
08:11.720 --> 08:12.840
It's been bothering me since high school.

190
08:12.840 --> 08:14.280
What is it?

191
08:14.520 --> 08:15.760
Did you two ever date?

192
08:19.400 --> 08:20.600
No.

193
08:20.680 --> 08:21.520
Impossible. Look.

194
08:21.520 --> 08:22.520
They won't admit it.

195
08:22.520 --> 08:24.720
A guilty conscience needs no accuser, right?

196
08:24.720 --> 08:25.440
But when we were in school,

197
08:25.440 --> 08:27.600
I thought you two were a perfect match.

198
08:27.600 --> 08:28.400
No, Zhao Jia.

199
08:28.880 --> 08:30.440
You still look like a perfect match now.

200
08:30.440 --> 08:31.880
Yes, we all think so.

201
08:31.880 --> 08:32.760
Zhao Jia,

202
08:33.000 --> 08:35.280
what could you see when you were in school?

203
08:35.280 --> 08:37.340
Weren't you highly myopic back then?

204
08:37.840 --> 08:38.200
Exactly.

205
08:38.200 --> 08:39.840
Otherwise, how could she have fallen for Cheng Fei?

206
08:39.840 --> 08:40.919
Come on.

207
08:41.200 --> 08:41.880
Come on.

208
08:42.000 --> 08:42.880
Come on.

209
08:44.120 --> 08:45.000
Let's see which of you two

210
08:45.000 --> 08:46.560
can win this case, right?

211
08:47.320 --> 08:48.840
Lian, you have to treat me to a meal.

212
08:48.840 --> 08:50.280
No problem, my treat.

213
08:50.280 --> 08:52.140
I only found out about this today.

214
08:57.400 --> 08:59.840
My nephew is so capable.

215
08:59.840 --> 09:01.200
Uncle, I'm fast.

216
09:01.280 --> 09:02.560
Stop working. Come here.

217
09:02.560 --> 09:04.000
Let me chat with you. Come.

218
09:04.000 --> 09:04.320
Sit.

219
09:07.480 --> 09:08.680
You're so lovable.

220
09:11.240 --> 09:11.640
No.

221
09:11.640 --> 09:14.200
What's wrong, Uncle? You're scaring me by looking at me like that.

222
09:14.200 --> 09:16.600
What are you afraid of? Am I going to eat you?

223
09:18.280 --> 09:20.840
This skill of memorizing laws,

224
09:20.840 --> 09:22.570
why didn't you show it earlier?

225
09:23.200 --> 09:25.040
Uncle, I...

226
09:25.080 --> 09:26.400
The day you picked me up at the train station,

227
09:26.400 --> 09:28.720
I told you I had a good memory. Did you forget?

228
09:28.720 --> 09:30.440
You said it so subtly.

229
09:30.760 --> 09:32.640
That was close. We almost missed this opportunity.

230
09:32.640 --> 09:34.960
Alright, you've passed my test.

231
09:35.400 --> 09:36.400
Really, Uncle?

232
09:36.400 --> 09:37.840
Would I lie to you?

233
09:38.080 --> 09:40.400
Now, we just need Xiao Longnv to nod.

234
09:40.720 --> 09:42.880
I'll create more opportunities for you.

235
09:42.880 --> 09:44.040
When you get the chance,

236
09:44.040 --> 09:46.080
you should show off well, okay?

237
09:46.200 --> 09:46.880
Okay.

238
09:46.880 --> 09:47.840
Don't forget.

239
09:47.880 --> 09:50.610
Whose side are you on after entering the law firm?

240
09:51.720 --> 09:52.720
I won't forget.

241
09:52.720 --> 09:54.180
I'm on the law firm's side.

242
09:55.160 --> 09:56.400
You're on my side.

243
09:56.640 --> 09:57.760
Dong Beihu's side.

244
09:58.640 --> 09:59.400
Understand?

245
10:00.280 --> 10:01.840
Understood. We're related by blood.

246
10:01.840 --> 10:02.400
Right.

247
10:02.400 --> 10:02.960
Bye.

248
10:02.960 --> 10:04.640
My treat next time. Old Lian, my treat.

249
10:04.640 --> 10:05.400
It's settled then.

250
10:05.400 --> 10:06.040
Okay.

251
10:06.280 --> 10:06.920
Bye.

252
10:06.920 --> 10:08.160
I'm taking the drunk girl home.

253
10:08.160 --> 10:08.880
Bye. Bye. Let's go.

254
10:08.880 --> 10:09.520
Bye.

255
10:09.560 --> 10:10.560
Drive slowly.

256
10:13.760 --> 10:15.280
Let's go. I'll take you back.

257
10:15.280 --> 10:17.640
No, we're opponents now.

258
10:17.680 --> 10:18.520
Keep some

259
10:18.520 --> 10:20.160
distance that opponents should have.

260
10:20.160 --> 10:21.040
All right.

261
10:21.880 --> 10:24.160
See you in court then.

262
10:25.160 --> 10:26.920
Let's have a good match.

263
10:27.560 --> 10:29.680
Don't worry, I won't show any mercy.

264
10:31.680 --> 10:32.740
What are you doing?

265
10:33.400 --> 10:34.160
Nothing.

266
10:36.080 --> 10:37.640
You're so annoying.

267
10:43.560 --> 10:44.760
What are you doing?

268
10:45.280 --> 10:47.080
Lawyer Xiao is so busy every day.

269
10:47.840 --> 10:50.400
Are insurance cases that easy to win?

270
10:50.680 --> 10:51.880
What did you find?

271
10:52.280 --> 10:55.000
Documents? This must have taken a lot of effort.

272
10:55.280 --> 10:55.880
What nonsense.

273
10:55.880 --> 10:58.520
You'd even die to work with Lawyer Xiao?

274
10:58.560 --> 10:59.920
Don't say that, kid.

275
11:00.160 --> 11:01.090
Come in quickly.

276
11:01.680 --> 11:03.680
What kind of act are you putting on here?

277
11:03.680 --> 11:04.160
No, no.

278
11:04.160 --> 11:05.800
Luo Zhi is so enthusiastic about his work.

279
11:05.800 --> 11:06.760
I couldn't stop him. Hurry.

280
11:06.760 --> 11:07.620
Hurry up and go.

281
11:08.920 --> 11:09.800
Ms. Xiao.

282
11:09.800 --> 11:12.560
I found some cases on insurance.

283
11:12.800 --> 11:14.560
I don't know if they will help you.

284
11:14.560 --> 11:15.690
You found all these?

285
11:16.040 --> 11:16.840
Thanks for your hard work.

286
11:16.840 --> 11:17.280
Thank you.

287
11:17.280 --> 11:19.040
What are you thanking him for? We're all family.

288
11:19.040 --> 11:21.240
Feel free to ask him for help from now on.

289
11:21.400 --> 11:23.060
What are you surprised about?

290
11:23.080 --> 11:23.840
Sister Long.

291
11:24.200 --> 11:25.640
The opposing lawyer for this insurance case is...

292
11:25.640 --> 11:26.800
Li Xin.

293
11:27.040 --> 11:28.280
You knew?

294
11:28.680 --> 11:30.680
Sister, don't feel pressured.

295
11:31.040 --> 11:32.280
What do you mean I feel pressured?

296
11:32.280 --> 11:34.680
What you're saying is so funny.

297
11:34.800 --> 11:36.320
He should be the one feeling pressured to face me.

298
11:36.320 --> 11:37.600
You really don't know how to chat.

299
11:37.600 --> 11:38.440
Miao'er, I've noticed...

300
11:38.440 --> 11:38.800
It's not me.

301
11:38.800 --> 11:40.060
I'm going out for a bit.

302
11:40.720 --> 11:41.450
Take it easy.

303
11:49.800 --> 11:52.720
Who is that Li Xinyi?

304
11:53.720 --> 11:56.320
Is Lawyer Li Xinyi pretty good?

305
11:56.360 --> 11:57.440
Good or not,

306
11:57.440 --> 11:58.720
beating him is just a game.

307
11:58.720 --> 12:00.040
Rowing him is just a boat.

308
12:00.040 --> 12:01.200
Flipping him is just a card.

309
12:01.200 --> 12:02.530
Spending him is just...

310
12:04.440 --> 12:06.970
Li Xinyi is a piece of cake. I'll take him down.

311
12:08.840 --> 12:10.000
That didn't rhyme.

312
12:10.080 --> 12:11.720
His name is Li Xin. Li Xin.

313
12:11.800 --> 12:12.720
Did you hear me?

314
12:13.080 --> 12:13.720
Who?

315
12:13.840 --> 12:15.200
Lawyer Xiao Longnv.

316
12:18.480 --> 12:19.340
Are you scared?

317
12:19.720 --> 12:19.840
Feng.

318
12:19.840 --> 12:21.440
What's there to be scared of?

319
12:21.440 --> 12:23.200
She hasn't handled a single insurance case in our firm.

320
12:23.200 --> 12:24.440
Why should I be scared?

321
12:24.440 --> 12:26.370
I must take her down a peg this time.

322
12:27.040 --> 12:28.700
Judging from the indictment,

323
12:28.800 --> 12:30.320
her main point of attack is

324
12:30.600 --> 12:31.720
purulent meningitis.

325
12:31.720 --> 12:32.560
Layman.

326
12:33.200 --> 12:34.080
She's a layman.

327
12:35.080 --> 12:36.080
In Shengkang's policy,

328
12:36.080 --> 12:37.440
what meets the compensation conditions

329
12:37.440 --> 12:39.700
is the sequelae of purulent meningitis.

330
12:39.840 --> 12:40.960
This and purulent meningitis

331
12:40.960 --> 12:42.080
are two completely different things.

332
12:42.080 --> 12:43.840
How could she write her real intention of attack

333
12:43.840 --> 12:44.720
on it?

334
12:46.720 --> 12:47.320
Bowen,

335
12:47.440 --> 12:49.600
sort out the parts of the contract related to the dispute in this case

336
12:49.600 --> 12:51.960
and the medical records of the insured.

337
12:52.440 --> 12:53.040
Ding Chao,

338
12:53.040 --> 12:54.320
search the court's

339
12:54.320 --> 12:56.960
personal insurance claims cases in the past three years,

340
12:56.960 --> 12:58.080
and summarize them.

341
12:58.080 --> 12:58.740
No problem.

342
12:58.840 --> 12:59.440
Lanya,

343
12:59.920 --> 13:01.400
check Shengkang Insurance's internal

344
13:01.400 --> 13:02.280
claims files.

345
13:02.600 --> 13:03.960
See if there are any similar cases.

346
13:03.960 --> 13:04.680
Okay.

347
13:05.200 --> 13:05.840
Everyone,

348
13:06.600 --> 13:07.800
this lawsuit is about

349
13:07.800 --> 13:09.680
whether we can have a long-term cooperation

350
13:09.680 --> 13:11.210
with Shengkang Insurance.

351
13:11.280 --> 13:12.680
So don't take it lightly.

352
13:12.800 --> 13:13.600
Copy that.

353
13:17.160 --> 13:17.760
Longnv.

354
13:18.480 --> 13:19.160
Monitor.

355
13:20.800 --> 13:22.560
Why are your eyes so red?

356
13:22.560 --> 13:24.020
Did you stay up late again?

357
13:24.160 --> 13:26.040
There's a case going to court soon.

358
13:26.040 --> 13:27.400
The files alone fill five or six boxes.

359
13:27.400 --> 13:28.520
But you can't stay up like this.

360
13:28.520 --> 13:29.640
How can your body take it?

361
13:29.640 --> 13:31.570
It's fine. Tell me about your case.

362
13:32.120 --> 13:32.840
As you know,

363
13:33.480 --> 13:35.240
I've never handled an insurance case before.

364
13:35.240 --> 13:37.570
I feel like my thoughts aren't very clear,

365
13:37.600 --> 13:39.040
so I wanted to ask for your help.

366
13:39.040 --> 13:40.640
I've read the materials you gave me.

367
13:40.640 --> 13:42.520
The main dispute between the two parties is over

368
13:42.520 --> 13:44.480
the compensation definition for purulent meningitis, right?

369
13:44.480 --> 13:44.960
Yes.

370
13:45.520 --> 13:46.520
The keywords on this,

371
13:46.520 --> 13:47.800
I've highlighted them for you.

372
13:47.800 --> 13:49.200
That's my class monitor.

373
13:49.280 --> 13:50.520
Do you know who the opposing lawyer is?

374
13:50.520 --> 13:51.280
Li Xin.

375
13:52.880 --> 13:54.880
Then this is a clash of titans.

376
13:55.000 --> 13:56.880
I ran into Lawyer Li once before.

377
13:57.040 --> 13:58.280
He's steady, accurate, and ruthless.

378
13:58.280 --> 13:59.640
I lost miserably.

379
13:59.640 --> 14:00.640
That's why

380
14:00.760 --> 14:03.520
what I have on hand now is not enough.

381
14:03.640 --> 14:05.700
I want to find another breakthrough.

382
14:06.040 --> 14:07.520
When I handled medical cases before,

383
14:07.520 --> 14:09.280
I found that hospitals keep

384
14:09.600 --> 14:12.040
a more detailed diagnosis and treatment log internally.

385
14:12.040 --> 14:13.120
Medical log.

386
14:13.120 --> 14:14.760
It's like a doctor's diary.

387
14:15.080 --> 14:16.360
It includes specific details

388
14:16.360 --> 14:17.890
during the rescue process.

389
14:18.120 --> 14:19.780
I think you can look into this.

390
14:26.040 --> 14:26.840
Director Lin.

391
14:27.160 --> 14:29.720
What does DIC mean?

392
14:29.720 --> 14:31.360
It's a medical term,

393
14:31.360 --> 14:33.820
disseminated intravascular coagulation.

394
14:34.280 --> 14:35.440
Simply put,

395
14:35.440 --> 14:38.360
the body's coagulation function is over-activated.

396
14:38.360 --> 14:40.360
Then what kind of situation

397
14:40.360 --> 14:42.640
would over-activate this coagulation function?

398
14:42.640 --> 14:44.880
Blood is the body's power source.

399
14:44.880 --> 14:46.760
When many diseases reach their terminal stage,

400
14:46.760 --> 14:48.640
especially when death is imminent,

401
14:48.640 --> 14:52.120
the body's coagulation function is automatically activated.

402
14:52.120 --> 14:53.640
Then it is possible to develop

403
14:53.640 --> 14:56.100
disseminated intravascular coagulation.

404
14:59.920 --> 15:00.650
Lawyer Xiao.

405
15:01.080 --> 15:02.520
Lawyer Xiao, what a coincidence.

406
15:02.520 --> 15:03.720
You move pretty fast.

407
15:03.920 --> 15:06.440
First time handling an insurance case, feeling unsure?

408
15:06.440 --> 15:07.720
Well, I saw you here.

409
15:07.720 --> 15:09.980
That instantly gave me full confidence.

410
15:28.840 --> 15:29.440
Come in.

411
15:30.360 --> 15:31.000
Lawyer Li.

412
15:32.400 --> 15:34.120
This is the patient's medical log.

413
15:34.120 --> 15:34.680
But Lawyer Xiao...

414
15:34.680 --> 15:36.810
She already got it one step ahead of us.

415
15:40.400 --> 15:41.160
Lawyer Li.

416
15:42.560 --> 15:43.560
Is Lawyer Xiao...

417
15:43.560 --> 15:45.490
Is she a very formidable opponent?

418
15:45.680 --> 15:47.340
No matter who the opponent is,

419
15:47.400 --> 15:49.240
we must be fully prepared.

420
15:53.160 --> 15:55.090
But she is indeed very formidable.

421
16:14.400 --> 16:15.800
Today is a pre-trial conference.

422
16:15.800 --> 16:17.520
Both sides just need to submit evidence.

423
16:17.520 --> 16:18.720
No need to be nervous.

424
16:26.760 --> 16:29.490
Will the plaintiff please present the evidence.

425
16:31.040 --> 16:33.000
At 3:00 AM on February 7th,

426
16:33.040 --> 16:36.840
Han Kexin suddenly experienced symptoms like convulsions at home.

427
16:37.000 --> 16:37.640
Doctor.

428
16:37.760 --> 16:40.120
What exactly is wrong with this child?

429
16:40.760 --> 16:42.760
This is as far as we can check.

430
16:43.240 --> 16:43.640
We suggest you

431
16:43.640 --> 16:45.520
transfer to a larger hospital.

432
16:50.920 --> 16:52.000
At 5:00 a.m.,

433
16:52.120 --> 16:53.650
Han Kexin was transferred.

434
16:53.760 --> 16:56.360
Upon admission, she had continuous convulsions and dilated pupils.

435
16:56.360 --> 16:57.680
Her pupillary light reflex was sluggish.

436
16:57.680 --> 17:00.240
She had a persistent high fever of 39 to 40 degrees,

437
17:00.240 --> 17:01.920
and her whole body was covered with purple patterns.

438
17:01.920 --> 17:03.280
Are you Han Kexin's family?

439
17:03.280 --> 17:03.800
How is she?

440
17:03.800 --> 17:05.680
The child has purulent meningitis.

441
17:05.680 --> 17:07.160
She is in critical condition now.

442
17:07.160 --> 17:08.240
This is a notice of critical condition.

443
17:08.240 --> 17:09.160
Please sign it.

444
17:10.680 --> 17:11.760
Please sign it quickly

445
17:11.760 --> 17:12.920
so we can save her.

446
17:14.400 --> 17:14.920
Yes.

447
17:15.800 --> 17:17.280
The above evidence proves

448
17:18.000 --> 17:20.920
that the insured ultimately died

449
17:20.920 --> 17:22.319
of purulent meningitis.

450
17:22.440 --> 17:24.839
Does the plaintiff have any other evidence to add?

451
17:24.839 --> 17:25.400
Yes.

452
17:25.760 --> 17:27.819
My core argument is the second point.

453
17:27.839 --> 17:29.200
The insured's condition

454
17:29.200 --> 17:31.720
meets another claim item in the policy,

455
17:31.760 --> 17:34.220
disseminated intravascular coagulation.

456
17:34.640 --> 17:35.040
Three.

457
17:35.440 --> 17:38.600
The insured meets the criteria for deep coma under critical illness.

458
17:38.600 --> 17:39.120
In summary,

459
17:39.120 --> 17:42.040
the above-mentioned diseases suffered by the insured, Han Kexin,

460
17:42.040 --> 17:43.800
had endangered her health,

461
17:43.800 --> 17:45.400
and she died after rescue efforts failed.

462
17:45.400 --> 17:47.360
It falls under Article 2 of the insurance contract,

463
17:47.360 --> 17:49.160
Paragraph 3 of Insurance Liability,

464
17:49.160 --> 17:51.360
as the critical illness stipulated in

465
17:51.360 --> 17:52.400
the critical illness insurance benefit.

466
17:52.400 --> 17:55.360
The defendant should pay the critical illness insurance benefit.

467
17:55.360 --> 17:57.360
Defendant, regarding the evidence presented by the plaintiff,

468
17:57.360 --> 18:00.090
please state your cross-examination opinions.

469
18:00.240 --> 18:02.160
We have no objection to the authenticity and legality

470
18:02.160 --> 18:04.560
of the medical records and treatment logs.

471
18:04.680 --> 18:07.040
We object to the second point of proof.

472
18:09.360 --> 18:11.400
According to Article 9, Clause 6 of the insurance contract,

473
18:11.400 --> 18:13.680
Item 69 on critical illnesses stipulates

474
18:13.680 --> 18:16.000
that disseminated intravascular coagulation

475
18:16.000 --> 18:19.680
must reach the middle or late clinical stage,

476
18:19.760 --> 18:22.720
and there must be a record of blood transfusion as a result.

477
18:22.720 --> 18:24.800
However, the treatment log provided by the plaintiff

478
18:24.800 --> 18:27.240
only shows disseminated intravascular coagulation,

479
18:27.240 --> 18:30.800
but does not indicate whether it is early, middle, or late stage,

480
18:30.800 --> 18:35.080
and it does not establish a causal relationship with the blood transfusion process.

481
18:35.080 --> 18:36.920
We object to the third point of proof.

482
18:36.920 --> 18:38.600
Deep coma refers to

483
18:38.600 --> 18:40.680
a loss of consciousness caused by

484
18:40.720 --> 18:41.520
illness or accidental injury,

485
18:41.520 --> 18:43.520
with continuous use of a ventilator

486
18:43.520 --> 18:46.120
and other life support systems

487
18:46.240 --> 18:47.960
for more than 96 hours.

488
18:48.720 --> 18:51.600
But the insured did not meet this standard.

489
18:51.600 --> 18:52.400
Your Honor,

490
18:52.680 --> 18:54.480
the reason the insured in this case

491
18:54.480 --> 18:56.960
used the ventilator for less than 96 hours

492
18:56.960 --> 18:58.000
is because the insured's condition

493
18:58.000 --> 18:59.840
was so severe that it resulted in death.

494
18:59.840 --> 19:02.400
Counsel for the plaintiff, we are currently in the evidence presentation phase.

495
19:02.400 --> 19:03.480
This is not the debate stage.

496
19:03.480 --> 19:05.200
Please pay attention to the order of speaking.

497
19:05.200 --> 19:06.880
Please note, Your Honor,

498
19:06.880 --> 19:08.440
the death of the insured

499
19:08.440 --> 19:11.160
and the cessation of the ventilator...

500
19:11.160 --> 19:12.120
the chronological order between them.

501
19:12.120 --> 19:12.800
Thank you.

502
19:13.960 --> 19:16.640
The medical and discharge records state

503
19:16.640 --> 19:18.360
that the child was in critical condition,

504
19:18.360 --> 19:21.640
and the family was informed of the condition.

505
19:21.680 --> 19:23.240
There was a risk of cardiac arrest

506
19:23.240 --> 19:25.360
and respiratory arrest at any time.

507
19:25.640 --> 19:27.440
The family expressed understanding

508
19:27.440 --> 19:29.440
and voluntarily gave up treatment,

509
19:29.680 --> 19:32.140
requesting discharge, which was reported.

510
19:36.200 --> 19:37.200
So it seems...

511
19:37.280 --> 19:40.160
The patient's family did not pursue active treatment.

512
19:40.160 --> 19:43.240
If our insurance company pays out the claim,

513
19:43.240 --> 19:44.680
could it be understood as

514
19:45.680 --> 19:47.480
encouraging such abandonment?

515
19:47.760 --> 19:48.960
Are you even human?

516
19:48.960 --> 19:50.080
Mr. Han, please calm down.

517
19:50.080 --> 19:50.480
Do you know

518
19:50.480 --> 19:52.120
what our family has been through these past few months?

519
19:52.120 --> 19:54.240
How dare you say I didn't try to save my child?

520
19:54.240 --> 19:55.920
Why wouldn't I save my child?

521
19:55.960 --> 19:56.880
You scumbag lawyer!

522
19:56.880 --> 19:58.160
You're not human!

523
19:58.360 --> 19:59.160
Your Honor,

524
19:59.360 --> 20:01.200
what the opposing counsel just said

525
20:01.200 --> 20:02.960
is an insult to my client.

526
20:03.400 --> 20:05.120
Plaintiff, please calm down.

527
20:16.920 --> 20:17.600
Li Xin.

528
20:26.280 --> 20:28.280
My client's child just passed away.

529
20:28.360 --> 20:29.160
You know that.

530
20:30.960 --> 20:32.440
You knew, yet you provoked him in court.

531
20:32.440 --> 20:33.640
What's your problem?

532
20:34.720 --> 20:36.480
I was just raising reasonable doubts

533
20:36.480 --> 20:38.080
within the limits of the law.

534
20:38.960 --> 20:40.880
But the law is not without compassion,

535
20:40.880 --> 20:42.720
and reason is not without humanity.

536
20:42.720 --> 20:44.760
Can't you have some empathy, Mr. Li?

537
20:44.760 --> 20:47.440
Ignoring obvious doubts in this case

538
20:48.360 --> 20:50.000
would be irresponsible to my client.

539
20:50.000 --> 20:52.440
If you have doubts, submit a written supplement.

540
20:52.440 --> 20:53.680
Provoking him in court,

541
20:53.680 --> 20:54.480
is that the only way

542
20:54.480 --> 20:56.960
you can find the truth, Mr. Li?

543
20:58.640 --> 20:59.440
You have your methods.

544
20:59.440 --> 21:00.640
I have mine.

545
21:01.680 --> 21:03.520
My goal wasn't to provoke him.

546
21:04.280 --> 21:06.010
I'm just doing what I have to do.

547
21:06.200 --> 21:07.240
Sorry, Ms. Xiao.

548
21:07.720 --> 21:09.980
I have something to do. I'll leave first.

549
21:33.000 --> 21:33.730
You're back.

550
21:34.240 --> 21:35.480
Drink up. Come on, drink up.

551
21:35.480 --> 21:36.920
Sea cucumber and chicken soup.

552
21:36.920 --> 21:38.160
It's so fresh.

553
21:38.680 --> 21:39.880
Where did the sea cucumber come from?

554
21:39.880 --> 21:42.800
It's the one Xin gave to Old Li a few days ago.

555
21:43.040 --> 21:44.000
Speaking of this kid,

556
21:44.000 --> 21:45.200
he's really thoughtful.

557
21:45.200 --> 21:46.160
How is he thoughtful?

558
21:46.160 --> 21:47.400
I won't eat the sea cucumber he gave us.

559
21:47.400 --> 21:48.640
Eating it will make me mindless.

560
21:48.640 --> 21:51.040
Come on. This is very nourishing, you know?

561
21:54.600 --> 21:56.080
What's wrong now?

562
21:56.120 --> 21:59.400
Dad, tell me, why is he so cold-blooded?

563
21:59.400 --> 22:01.160
He doesn't take after Uncle Li at all.

564
22:01.160 --> 22:01.960
Why wouldn't he?

565
22:01.960 --> 22:02.560
It's in his blood.

566
22:02.560 --> 22:03.400
What do you mean?

567
22:03.400 --> 22:04.960
Your Uncle Li is even more cold-blooded.

568
22:04.960 --> 22:06.160
Uncle Li is cold-blooded?

569
22:06.160 --> 22:07.200
When he arrested us back then,

570
22:07.200 --> 22:09.320
hands behind our backs, handcuffs on,

571
22:09.320 --> 22:10.120
he was completely impartial.

572
22:10.120 --> 22:12.200
But Xin is really a good kid.

573
22:12.320 --> 22:13.400
Why can't you stand him?

574
22:13.400 --> 22:15.440
My opinion of him is very objective.

575
22:15.480 --> 22:16.800
He's just cold-blooded.

576
22:16.800 --> 22:17.640
Are you angry?

577
22:19.320 --> 22:20.400
The best way to get back at him

578
22:20.400 --> 22:22.320
is to eat the sea cucumber he bought.

579
22:22.320 --> 22:23.320
What kind of idea is that?

580
22:23.320 --> 22:24.400
Really, you stewed it.

581
22:24.400 --> 22:27.130
Look, didn't Li Xin buy this little sea cucumber?

582
22:29.400 --> 22:31.260
It tastes like Li Xin when stewed.

583
22:31.320 --> 22:33.240
Eat it. Punish him.

584
22:34.080 --> 22:36.360
Some people have a sharp tongue but a soft heart.

585
22:36.360 --> 22:36.920
What they think in their hearts

586
22:36.920 --> 22:39.160
is completely different from what they say.

587
22:39.160 --> 22:40.200
Eat up.

588
22:40.200 --> 22:41.120
Okay.

589
22:42.560 --> 22:43.320
Coming.

590
22:45.640 --> 22:46.770
Don't you have a key?

591
22:52.680 --> 22:55.360
Look at you, always buying things from such expensive places.

592
22:55.360 --> 22:56.000
It's fine.

593
23:04.240 --> 23:05.100
Let me help you.

594
23:05.320 --> 23:06.120
No need.

595
23:06.120 --> 23:06.560
Come on.

596
23:06.560 --> 23:07.320
No need.

597
23:20.640 --> 23:21.640
Just answer it.

598
23:22.760 --> 23:23.800
It's no big deal.

599
23:24.720 --> 23:26.200
I just won't listen.

600
23:30.040 --> 23:30.400
Mom.

601
23:30.400 --> 23:32.320
Son, look.

602
23:33.000 --> 23:34.800
Jeffrey, he's your brother.

603
23:34.800 --> 23:35.400
Say hi.

604
23:35.400 --> 23:36.400
Hello.

605
23:39.400 --> 23:40.920
Wilson. Wilson is here.

606
23:41.200 --> 23:41.880
Li Xin.

607
23:41.880 --> 23:43.280
You look great.

608
23:43.400 --> 23:45.120
We were just talking about you.

609
23:45.120 --> 23:47.400
When are you coming to Canada?

610
23:47.480 --> 23:48.410
Thanks, Wilson.

611
23:49.600 --> 23:51.360
I'll definitely go when I have time.

612
23:51.360 --> 23:52.640
I'm going to get some water.

613
23:52.640 --> 23:53.700
See you later, Xin.

614
23:54.600 --> 23:55.400
Son.

615
23:56.040 --> 23:57.440
How have you been lately?

616
23:57.680 --> 23:58.410
Pretty good.

617
23:58.640 --> 23:59.400
I heard

618
23:59.720 --> 24:01.600
you got promoted to senior partner.

619
24:01.600 --> 24:02.920
Such good news.

620
24:02.920 --> 24:04.320
Why didn't you tell Mom?

621
24:04.600 --> 24:05.240
I saw it

622
24:05.240 --> 24:07.520
on your Honghu official account.

623
24:07.840 --> 24:08.960
I was too busy and forgot.

624
24:08.960 --> 24:10.840
Mom sent you a promotion gift.

625
24:10.840 --> 24:11.920
Did you get it?

626
24:12.160 --> 24:12.840
I got it.

627
24:12.840 --> 24:14.600
I haven't had time to open it yet.

628
24:14.600 --> 24:15.960
I'll open it when I get back today.

629
24:15.960 --> 24:17.620
Are you at Li Guochen's place?

630
24:17.960 --> 24:18.640
Yes.

631
24:19.120 --> 24:20.680
You go there quite often.

632
24:21.160 --> 24:23.080
He's enjoying life now.

633
24:23.960 --> 24:25.800
My dad is retired now.

634
24:25.800 --> 24:26.640
He's alone.

635
24:26.840 --> 24:27.600
Besides,

636
24:28.200 --> 24:29.640
isn't it my duty as a son?

637
24:31.160 --> 24:33.400
Mom, let's talk later.

638
24:33.400 --> 24:34.920
Take good care of yourself.

639
24:34.920 --> 24:35.720
You hear me?

640
24:35.840 --> 24:37.080
Don't work too hard.

641
24:37.160 --> 24:38.360
Bye.

642
24:46.160 --> 24:46.600
Done.

643
24:46.960 --> 24:47.800
Let me help you.

644
24:47.800 --> 24:48.160
No, thanks.

645
24:48.160 --> 24:49.400
I can do it.

646
24:52.480 --> 24:53.160
Then...

647
25:19.800 --> 25:21.400
Your Honor, please note

648
25:21.400 --> 25:23.080
the chronological order between

649
25:23.080 --> 25:25.720
the death of the insured

650
25:25.720 --> 25:26.600
and the removal of the ventilator.

651
25:26.600 --> 25:29.000
The medical and discharge records state that

652
25:29.000 --> 25:30.640
the child was in critical condition,

653
25:30.640 --> 25:33.840
